{"id":"b1542355-a4e8-49b4-b61e-832239a96b11","object":"chat.completion","created":1784822951,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    try:\\n        initial_state = case[\\\"initial_state\\\"]\\n        max_steps = case[\\\"max_steps\\\"]\\n        tool_observations = case[\\\"tool_observations\\\"]\\n        transitions = case[\\\"transitions\\\"]\\n    except KeyError as e:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required field: {e}\\\")\\n    if initial_state not in transitions:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"Initial state '{initial_state}' not found in transitions\\\")\\n    for state_name, state_data in transitions.items():\\n        if not isinstance(state_data, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Invalid state data for '{state_name}'\\\")\\n        kind = state_data.get(\\\"kind\\\")\\n        if kind not in (\\\"action\\\", \\\"final\\\"):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"State '{state_name}' has invalid kind '{kind}'\\\")\\n        if kind == \\\"action\\\":\\n            action = state_data.get(\\\"action\\\")\\n            if action not in tool_observations:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"State '{state_name}' references unknown tool '{action}'\\\")\\n            next_by_obs = state_data.get(\\\"next_by_observation\\\", {})\\n            for obs, next_state in next_by_obs.items():\\n                if next_state not in transitions:\\n                    raise ValueError(f\\\"State '{state_name}' next_by_observation maps to unknown state '{next_state}'\\\")\\n            default_next = state_data.get(\\\"default_next\\\")\\n            if default_next is not None and default_next not in transitions:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"State '{state_name}' default_next '{default_next}' not in transitions\\\")\\n    current_state = initial_state\\n    steps_taken = 0\\n    trace = []\\n    while steps_taken < max_steps:\\n        state_data = transitions[current_state]\\n        if state_data[\\\"kind\\\"] == \\\"final\\\":\\n            break\\n        action = state_data[\\\"action\\\"]\\n        observation = tool_observations[action]\\n        next_by_obs = state_data.get(\\\"next_by_observation\\\", {})\\n        default_next = state_data.get(\\\"default_next\\\")\\n        if observation in next_by_obs:\\n            next_state = next_by_obs[observation]\\n        else:\\n            next_state = default_next\\n            if next_state is None:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"No next state defined for observation '{observation}' and no default_next\\\")\\n        step = {\\n            \\\"state\\\": current_state,\\n            \\\"action\\\": action,\\n            \\\"observation\\\": observation,\\n            \\\"next_state\\\": next_state\\n        }\\n        trace.append(step)\\n        current_state = next_state\\n        steps_taken += 1\\n    final_state_data = transitions.get(current_state)\\n    if final_state_data and final_state_data[\\\"kind\\\"] == \\\"final\\\":\\n        status = \\\"completed\\\"\\n        final_value = final_state_data[\\\"value\\\"]\\n    else:\\n        status = \\\"max_steps_reached\\\"\\n        final_value = None\\n    return {\\n        \\\"status\\\": status,\\n        \\\"final_value\\\": final_value,\\n        \\\"trace\\\": trace\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a Python function `solve(case)` that implements a ReAct tool loop controller. The case payload includes:\n- initial_state: string\n- max_steps: integer\n- tool_observations: dict mapping tool names to their observation strings (deterministic)\n- transitions: dict mapping state names to objects. Each state object has:\n  - kind: either \"action\" or \"final\".\n  - If action: action (tool name), next_by_observation (dict mapping observation string to next state), default_next (string)\n  - If final: value (string, e.g., \"accepted\" or \"rejected\")\nWe need to simulate the loop:\n- Start at initial_state\n- For each step up to max_steps:\n  - If current state is final, stop (done). Return status \"completed\", final_value = that state's value, and trace (list of steps taken)\n  - If current state is action:\n    - Record step: state, action taken, observation, next state.\n    - Look up tool_observations for that action to get observation.\n    - Then in transitions, for current state's object, check next_by_observation for that observation. If found, next state = that. Else next state = default_next.\n    - Proceed to next state, increment step counter. If step count exceeds max_steps, stop and return status \"max_steps_reached\", final_value = None, trace so far.\n- Also need to handle missing tools or states? The problem says \"distinguish missing tools and states\" and \"raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case\". So we must validate:\n  - initial_state exists in transitions.\n  - For each action state, the action exists in tool_observations.\n  - For each action state, default_next exists in transitions? The spec says \"select the observation-specific successor or the default; distinguish missing tools and states.\" It also says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\" So we should check that the state referenced (both in next_by_observation and default_next) exist in transitions. If not, raise ValueError.\n  - Also check that max_steps is non-negative? Probably yes.\n  - Also check that kind is either \"action\" or \"final\".\n- Return a JSON-serializable object: probably a dict with keys: \"status\", \"final_value\", \"trace\". The trace should be a list of step dicts, each with fields: \"state\" (the state before action), \"action\", \"observation\", \"next_state\". The final step when reaching a final state should not be included as an action step; just the final_value from the final state. The problem says \"Stop on completion or max steps and return status, final value, and trace.\" So trace should include all action steps taken. If max_steps reached without reaching final, trace includes steps up to max_steps (the step that would have been taken but not completed? Actually we stop before exceeding max_steps. So we record steps for each successful action execution. If we exceed max_steps, we stop and don't record the step that would require the next action? We need to think: The loop: for step in range(max_steps): if current final -> break. else execute action, record step, update state. After loop, if we broke due to final, status completed; else status max_steps_reached. So trace includes steps that were actually executed. That's fine.\n- Also need to handle case where initial state is final: then trace is empty, status completed, final_value = that state's value.\n- Use only Python standard library.\n\nLet's write the function.\n\nWe'll parse case payload. It's passed as a dict? The function signature is `solve(case)`. The case is likely a dict with the payload inside. From fixtures, case has \"payload\" key. But the instruction says \"case\" is the case object. In the fixture, each case has \"case_id\" and \"payload\". So the function should probably accept the entire case dict? But the description says \"solve(case)\" where case is the payload? Let's look at the typical format: In many problems, the case is the payload itself. The fixture shows \"cases\" list with each having \"payload\". The instruction says \"attached public fixtures define input shapes only.\" It's ambiguous. However, the typical interpretation from these tasks is that the `solve` function receives the payload (the inner dict). Because they say \"Use only quantities present in the case payload.\" So I'll assume `case` is the payload dict, i.e., with keys: initial_state, max_steps, tool_observations, transitions. Also include _case_nonce? Not used. So we'll just handle the necessary keys.\n\nImplementation steps:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # extract fields\n    try:\n        initial_state = case[\"initial_state\"]\n        max_steps = case[\"max_steps\"]\n        tool_observations = case[\"tool_observations\"]\n        transitions = case[\"transitions\"]\n    except KeyError as e:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Missing required field: {e}\")\n\n    # Validate initial_state exists\n    if initial_state not in transitions:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Initial state '{initial_state}' not found in transitions\")\n\n    # Validate all states referenced in transitions exist\n    for state_name, state_data in transitions.items():\n        if not isinstance(state_data, dict):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid state data for '{state_name}'\")\n        kind = state_data.get(\"kind\")\n        if kind not in (\"action\", \"final\"):\n            raise ValueError(f\"State '{state_name}' has invalid kind '{kind}'\")\n        if kind == \"action\":\n            action = state_data.get(\"action\")\n            if action not in tool_observations:\n                raise ValueError(f\"State '{state_name}' references unknown tool '{action}'\")\n            # Validate next_by_observation values exist\n            next_by_obs = state_data.get(\"next_by_observation\", {})\n            for obs, next_state in next_by_obs.items():\n                if next_state not in transitions:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"State '{state_name}' next_by_observation maps to unknown state '{next_state}'\")\n            default_next = state_data.get(\"default_next\")\n            if default_next is not None and default_next not in transitions:\n                raise ValueError(f\"State '{state_name}' default_next '{default_next}' not in transitions\")\n        # For final, no further validation needed\n\n    # Simulation\n    current_state = initial_state\n    steps_taken = 0\n    trace = []\n\n    while steps_taken < max_steps:\n        state_data = transitions[current_state]\n        if state_data[\"kind\"] == \"final\":\n            break\n        # action state\n        action = state_data[\"action\"]\n        observation = tool_observations[action]\n        next_by_obs = state_data.get(\"next_by_observation\", {})\n        default_next = state_data.get(\"default_next\")\n        if observation in next_by_obs:\n            next_state = next_by_obs[observation]\n        else:\n            next_state = default_next\n            if next_state is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"No next state defined for observation '{observation}' and no default_next\")\n        # Record step\n        step = {\n            \"state\": current_state,\n            \"action\": action,\n            \"observation\": observation,\n            \"next_state\": next_state\n        }\n        trace.append(step)\n        current_state = next_state\n        steps_taken += 1\n\n    # After loop, determine status and final_value\n    final_state_data = transitions.get(current_state)\n    if final_state_data and final_state_data[\"kind\"] == \"final\":\n        status = \"completed\"\n        final_value = final_state_data[\"value\"]\n    else:\n        status = \"max_steps_reached\"\n        final_value = None\n\n    result = {\n        \"status\": status,\n        \"final_value\": final_value,\n        \"trace\": trace\n    }\n    return result\n\nCheck: The problem says \"return only JSON-serializable values with the exact named fields.\" So we must return a dict with those keys. Also \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case\". We do that.\n\nEdge cases: initial_state final; max_steps=0; invalid tool; etc.\n\nNow, output must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a JSON string. Escape appropriately.\n\nWe need to ensure no extra spaces, no markdown.\n\nWrite the function as a string with newlines escaped.\n\nLet's produce the JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1265,"compl